<section>
  <title>Course Description and Goal</title>
    <p><alert>MATH 123 Introduction to Functions</alert> (Gen. Ed. satisfying Core Math or Domain II-A requirements)</p>
    <p>An exploration of numerical, graphical, and symbolic approaches to function concepts with emphasis on real-world applications, modeling, and problem-solving skills. Topics include polynomial and rational functions, equations and inequalities, systems of linear equations, and the connection between functions and their graphs.  This course includes an additional a one-hour per week lecture recitation. Topics may vary by section at the discretion of the instructor with the goal of supporting students' readiness for, and success, in the lecture course.</p>
    <p><em>Prerequisite:</em> Satisfactory mathematics placement.</p>
</section>